=1 1 13
+    ARM port of KE/MIPS/ALIGNEM.C. ARMv7 performs the unaligned loads and
+    stores of a single word or halfword in hardware. Those of several words,
+    LDM, STM, PUSH, POP, LDRD and STRD, and those of the floating point and
+    SIMD unit, VLDR, VSTR, VLDM, VSTM, VPUSH, VPOP, and VLD1 and VST1 of
+    multiple elements, take an alignment fault (ke\trapc.c) at an address
+    that is not word aligned, or not aligned as a VLD1 or VST1 states.
+    Microsoft C for ARM moves structures, doublewords and the blocks of
+    memcpy with them as the types of their pointers allow. They are
+    emulated here in Thumb state, in user and in kernel mode, as the Alpha
+    and PowerPC kernels emulate theirs (ke\exceptn.c). The exclusive loads
+    and stores are not: their reference cannot be made atomic.
=1 13 14
